/**
 * riya-game — Riya — a math journey GAME with real physics, structured as an app: a collection of orbitals, one per world, plus a menu. Riya is a dot, a point in space with MASS: the player pushes it with arrows / WASD (hold to accelerate — keyMap/keyUpMap on the math-canvas) or taps the d-pad (velocity impulses), and the std-motion-body authority integrates gravity, acceleration, speed, damping, and walls every 50ms. Seven worlds climb the math ladder: the number line (/riya-line — coast and brake onto the ★ numbers), functions (/riya-curve — riya rides y = 0.25x² − 4, the rule picks your height), the derivative (/riya-slope — the hill's slope pushes back through motion-body's bias field; park where slope = 0), the turning points (/riya-peak — a cubic's hilltop and valley, both flat spots of f(x) = 0.5x³ − 1.5x), the limit (/riya-limit — ride f(x) = 8/x toward the wall at x = 0 and watch the f(x) chip explode), the exponential (/riya-expo — the doubling curve 2^(x/2) − 1, flat then a rocket), and the integral (/riya-area — walk the strip, paint every column, watch area = … add up). Numbers are always on screen: tick labels on every axis and live HUD chips (x, v, f(x), slope, area) next to the ★ score, a velocity arrow on riya, and the tangent line under it on the slope world. EVENT HYGIENE (learned the hard way): the client runtime drains its actor queue in FIFO, so a per-tick event subscription floods it and everything lags — this game therefore keeps ticks SET-ONLY (motion integrates; the play trait's gameTick collects stars / paints strips / writes the hill bias directly onto the shared entity) and reserves events for sparse, meaningful occurrences: keydown/keyup thrust, d-pad impulses, a star collected (BURST + PROGRESS), the gate's GAME_END. Each world composes std-motion-body + std-objective-flow + std-fx-particles with events renamed per world; collection runs in the play trait's gameTick because std-objective-reach's contract is discrete HERO_STEPPED steps, not continuous motion (see Almadar_Std_Game_Gaps.md). RiyaMenuOrbital (/riya) is the shell: title plus a button per world that (navigate ...)s into it. Clearing a world pops its clear overlay; Next ▶ navigates to the next world's page — and the final world's overlay is the RIYA COMPLETE celebration, returning to the menu. CONFLICT LAYER (v5.1): every good game needs an obstacle, and in riya the obstacle is the math itself — the misconception made physical. The LIMIT world's pole is a hazard: cross the danger line at x = 0.85 and the asymptote flings riya back and takes the last collected ★ (inDanger edge-guard so one entry = one penalty). The DOUBLING world has an antagonist: a second motion-body (the ghost, labeled 2^n) steered by the gameTick toward riya with acceleration ghostThrust·2^(stars held) — every ★ you carry doubles its hunger; a catch costs the last ★ and teleports the ghost back to its spawn (ghostArmed re-arm hysteresis at rearmDistance 2 prevents chain-drains). The AREA world's final ★ is a concept gate: gray and uncollectible until all 16 strips are painted — you cannot finish before the whole sum is laid down. (Pages are mount-scoped in the playground runtime, so cross-page run state like a persistent star bank would need a persistence-backed entity — out of scope; each world's HUD tracks its own ★ score.)
