app riya-game "5.1.0"
"Riya — a math journey GAME with real physics, structured as an app: a collection of orbitals, one per world, plus a menu. Riya is a dot, a point in space with MASS: the player pushes it with arrows / WASD (hold to accelerate — keyMap/keyUpMap on the math-canvas) or taps the d-pad (velocity impulses), and the std-motion-body authority integrates gravity, acceleration, speed, damping, and walls every 50ms. Seven worlds climb the math ladder: the number line (/riya-line — coast and brake onto the ★ numbers), functions (/riya-curve — riya rides y = 0.25x² − 4, the rule picks your height), the derivative (/riya-slope — the hill's slope pushes back through motion-body's bias field; park where slope = 0), the turning points (/riya-peak — a cubic's hilltop and valley, both flat spots of f(x) = 0.5x³ − 1.5x), the limit (/riya-limit — ride f(x) = 8/x toward the wall at x = 0 and watch the f(x) chip explode), the exponential (/riya-expo — the doubling curve 2^(x/2) − 1, flat then a rocket), and the integral (/riya-area — walk the strip, paint every column, watch area = … add up). Numbers are always on screen: tick labels on every axis and live HUD chips (x, v, f(x), slope, area) next to the ★ score, a velocity arrow on riya, and the tangent line under it on the slope world. EVENT HYGIENE (learned the hard way): the client runtime drains its actor queue in FIFO, so a per-tick event subscription floods it and everything lags — this game therefore keeps ticks SET-ONLY (motion integrates; the play trait's gameTick collects stars / paints strips / writes the hill bias directly onto the shared entity) and reserves events for sparse, meaningful occurrences: keydown/keyup thrust, d-pad impulses, a star collected (BURST + PROGRESS), the gate's GAME_END. Each world composes std-motion-body + std-objective-flow + std-fx-particles with events renamed per world; collection runs in the play trait's gameTick because std-objective-reach's contract is discrete HERO_STEPPED steps, not continuous motion (see Almadar_Std_Game_Gaps.md). RiyaMenuOrbital (/riya) is the shell: title plus a button per world that (navigate ...)s into it. Clearing a world pops its clear overlay; Next ▶ navigates to the next world's page — and the final world's overlay is the RIYA COMPLETE celebration, returning to the menu. CONFLICT LAYER (v5.1): every good game needs an obstacle, and in riya the obstacle is the math itself — the misconception made physical. The LIMIT world's pole is a hazard: cross the danger line at x = 0.85 and the asymptote flings riya back and takes the last collected ★ (inDanger edge-guard so one entry = one penalty). The DOUBLING world has an antagonist: a second motion-body (the ghost, labeled 2^n) steered by the gameTick toward riya with acceleration ghostThrust·2^(stars held) — every ★ you carry doubles its hunger; a catch costs the last ★ and teleports the ghost back to its spawn (ghostArmed re-arm hysteresis at rearmDistance 2 prevents chain-drains). The AREA world's final ★ is a concept gate: gray and uncollectible until all 16 strips are painted — you cannot finish before the whole sum is laid down. (Pages are mount-scoped in the playground runtime, so cross-page run state like a persistent star bank would need a persistence-backed entity — out of scope; each world's HUD tracks its own ★ score.)"

;; ============================================================================
;; PERSONAS + USER STORIES
;;
;; Read these before changing anything here, and walk them end to end after.
;;
;; MAYA, 9 — the player. Numbers are abstract to her; games are not. She
;; learns by feel: push, coast, overshoot, correct. She has never seen
;; f(x), dy/dx, or ∫ — this game is her first contact.
;;
;; HER TEACHER — the non-player stakeholder. Two standing requirements:
;; every world teaches ONE honest math idea, and the numbers are ALWAYS
;; visible on screen (no hidden state) — tick labels on the axes, live
;; readout chips, and the quantity of the world (position / f(x) / slope /
;; area) named and updating as riya moves.
;;
;; WORLD 1 · THE LINE — "position IS a number."
;;   1. I hold → and riya speeds up; I let go and it coasts to a stop — I
;;      feel acceleration and friction, not teleport-steps.
;;        WORKS. keydown sets holding=±1 and emits THRUST (guarded on
;;        holding-change so OS key-repeat can't flood); keyup zeroes it;
;;        motion-body's 50ms tick integrates ax into vx (capped by
;;        maxSpeed) and damping 0.94 bleeds vx each tick.
;;   2. I always see WHERE riya is as a number, and the line under it has
;;      numbered ticks — negative on the left, positive on the right.
;;        WORKS. showTickLabels paints axis numbers; HUD chips show
;;        x = … and v = … (math/round 1) every render tick.
;;   3. I'm told "catch the ★ at −6" and must brake in time — overshooting
;;      means turning around; negative numbers become PLACES.
;;        WORKS. Stars sit at x = −6, 3, 7 in world coordinates; the play
;;        trait's 50ms gameTick collects any star within reachRadius 0.6
;;        (sparse BURST + PROGRESS only on a catch); inertia makes braking
;;        the skill.
;;
;; WORLD 2 · THE CURVE — "a function is a rule that picks your height."
;;   4. Riya rides the curve — I steer only left/right; the rule
;;      y = 0.25x² − 4 decides my height and I watch f(x) = … change.
;;        WORKS. Physics is 1D (x only); the render and the collection math
;;        both map x → f(x), so riya is always painted and scored ON the
;;        curve; a HUD chip shows f(x) = math/round(f(x), 1).
;;   5. Stars sit exactly where the curve crosses zero and at its bottom,
;;      so I start predicting the curve's shape to plan my route.
;;        WORKS. Stars at (−4, 0), (0, −4), (4, 0) — the two roots and the
;;        vertex of 0.25x² − 4; the full curve is drawn from 129 samples.
;;
;; WORLD 3 · THE SLOPE — "steepness is a number you can feel."
;;   6. Climbing slows riya, descending speeds it up — I FEEL the slope as
;;      a push, while the slope number and the tangent line under riya make
;;      the same thing visible.
;;        WORKS. The play trait's gameTick emits SET_BIAS = −hillGravity·
;;        f′(x) each tick (motion-body adds the bias field to every body's
;;        acceleration each integration step); a HUD chip shows
;;        slope = … and a tangent segment is drawn through riya.
;;   7. I hunt the flat spots — hilltop and valley, where slope = 0 — and
;;      park riya on them.
;;        WORKS. Stars at (±π, ±3) — the critical points of f; thrust 12
;;        always beats the max hill push 5·1.5 = 7.5, so parking is skill,
;;        not luck.
;;
;; WORLD 4 · THE AREA — "area adds up."
;;   8. Every strip riya walks past gets painted under the ramp and the
;;      area = … number grows — the total is visibly a sum of little pieces.
;;        WORKS. The gameTick appends one unit-width bar per strip crossed
;;        (16 strips over x ∈ [−8, 8], midpoint heights of f(x) =
;;        0.25x + 3) and accumulates area += height·1; chips show area = …
;;        and strips = n. Midpoint rule is exact for linear f: the final
;;        number 48 IS the integral.
;;   9. Reaching the right wall with the whole region painted completes
;;      riya's journey.
;;        WORKS. The last ★ sits at (8, 0); the gameTick collects it, the
;;        gate resolves won, and the overlay is the RIYA COMPLETE banner
;;        back to the menu.
;;
;; WORLD 5 · THE PEAK — "a curvy rule has flat spots at its top and bottom."
;;  10. Climbing the cubic slows riya and descending speeds it up, like the
;;      slope world — but now the rule bends twice, so there are TWO flat
;;      spots: the hilltop and the valley.
;;        WORKS. f(x) = 0.5x³ − 1.5x; the gameTick emits PEAK_BIAS =
;;        −hillGravity·f′(x) each tick with f′(x) = 1.5x² − 1.5; thrust 14
;;        always beats the max push 2·5.76 = 11.5 inside the ±2.2 walls.
;;  11. I ride over the hilltop (−1, 1) and the valley (1, −1) to catch the
;;      ★s — and the slope chip reads 0 exactly there.
;;        WORKS. Stars at the two critical points; the HUD slope chip shows
;;        f′(x) = math/round(1.5x² − 1.5, 1); a tangent segment is drawn
;;        through riya; collection is pass-through within reachRadius 0.6.
;;
;; WORLD 6 · THE LIMIT — "closer and closer, never arriving."
;;  12. Riya rides f(x) = 8/x; the wall at x = 0.6 stops me before x = 0,
;;      but every step left makes the f(x) chip grow — 8, 13, 16 … I feel
;;      the curve run away from me.
;;        WORKS. Physics is 1D (x only); render and collection map x → 8/x;
;;        motion walls xMin 0.6 keep the pole unreachable; the HUD f(x) chip
;;        shows math/round(8/x, 1) every render tick.
;;  13. The ★s sit on the curve at (1, 8), (2, 4), (4, 2), (8, 1) — the
;;      highest one guards the approach to the wall.
;;        WORKS. Star positions are exact points of 8/x; the vertical line
;;        x = 0 is drawn in red as the asymptote the curve never touches.
;;
;; WORLD 7 · THE DOUBLING — "growth that outruns everything."
;;  14. Riya rides f(x) = 2^(x/2) − 1; every 2 steps right the height
;;      doubles — flat on the left, a rocket on the right.
;;        WORKS. Render and collection map x → 2^(x/2) − 1 (math/pow); the
;;        HUD f(x) chip shows the doubling as riya moves.
;;  15. The ★s sit at heights 0, 1, 3, 7 — one short of 1, 2, 4, 8 — so I
;;      catch the powers of two in order and feel their spacing stretch.
;;        WORKS. Stars at (0, 0), (2, 1), (4, 3), (6, 7) — exact points of
;;        2^(x/2) − 1; collection is pass-through within reachRadius 0.6.
;;
;; CONFLICT LAYER — "the math itself is the obstacle."
;;  16. THE POLE BITES (limit hazard). If I greedily push past the top ★
;;      toward x = 0, the curve flings riya back and takes my last ★ — I
;;      learn the asymptote is not a place you can stand.
;;        WORKS. The gameTick detects entry past dangerX 0.85 (edge-guarded
;;        by inDanger so one entry costs exactly one ★): the last collected
;;        star respawns (score −1, objectivesLeft +1, red "-1 ★" burst) and
;;        every tick inside the zone applies flingImpulse 6 away from the
;;        pole. dangerX sits below the top star's collection window (~0.93),
;;        so grabbing the ★ never triggers the hazard.
;;  17. GROWTH HUNTS YOU (doubling antagonist). A purple ghost rides the
;;      curve behind riya, and every ★ I hold doubles its hunger — dawdle
;;      and it catches me, taking my last ★.
;;        WORKS. The ghost is a second body in the same motion-body
;;        authority; the gameTick emits EXPO_THRUST for it each tick with
;;        ax = sign(hx−gx)·ghostThrust·2^score (per-tick intent, the
;;        slope-world SET_BIAS precedent). A catch (manhattan along the
;;        curve < 0.5) respawns the last ★ and teleports the ghost to its
;;        spawn; ghostArmed re-arms only beyond rearmDistance 2, so a
;;        cornered player can't be chain-drained. The HUD chip "2^n" shows
;;        the live multiplier 1, 2, 4, 8 — the exponent is on screen.
;;  18. NO SUM, NO STAR (area gate). The final ★ is gray and refuses to be
;;      collected until every strip is painted — I cannot finish before the
;;      whole sum is laid down.
;;        WORKS. The collection filter excludes finalStarId while painted <
;;        16 and the star renders gray (#64748b) instead of gold; painting
;;        the 16th strip (hx > 7) unlocks it, and reaching x = 8 collects
;;        it for the win.
;;
;; SHELL
;;  19. From the menu I pick any world; clearing one pops a banner and
;;      Next ▶ carries me to the next math idea.
;;        WORKS. RiyaMenuOrbital buttons (navigate …) to each world page;
;;        the gate's result != none drives the overlay in every render.
;;  20. Keyboard (hold arrows/WASD to push) and d-pad taps (nudge
;;      impulses) both drive riya.
;;        WORKS. math-canvas keyMap/keyUpMap emit per-world PUSH intents
;;        (holding-change-guarded THRUST); control-grid directionEvents
;;        emit per-world PAD intents applied as IMPULSE velocity kicks.
;; ============================================================================

orbital RiyaMenuOrbital {

  entity RiyaMenuItem [runtime] {
    id : string!
  }

  trait RiyaMenu -> @rebindable RiyaMenuItem [interaction, instance] {
    initial: idle

    state idle {
      INIT -> idle
        (render-ui main {
          type: box
          padding: md
          children: [
            { type: stack, direction: vertical, gap: md, children: [
                { type: typography, variant: h4, content: @config.gameTitle },
                { type: stack, direction: horizontal, gap: sm, children: [
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_LINE, label: "1 · The Line", variant: primary },
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_CURVE, label: "2 · The Curve", variant: primary },
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_SLOPE, label: "3 · The Slope", variant: primary },
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_PEAK, label: "4 · The Peak", variant: primary }
                  ] },
                { type: stack, direction: horizontal, gap: sm, children: [
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_LIMIT, label: "5 · The Limit", variant: primary },
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_EXPO, label: "6 · The Doubling", variant: primary },
                    { type: button, action: PLAY_AREA, label: "7 · The Area", variant: primary }
                  ] }
              ] }
          ]
        })

      PLAY_LINE -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-line")

      PLAY_CURVE -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-curve")

      PLAY_SLOPE -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-slope")

      PLAY_PEAK -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-peak")

      PLAY_LIMIT -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-limit")

      PLAY_EXPO -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-expo")

      PLAY_AREA -> idle
        (navigate "/riya-area")

    }


    emits {
      PLAY_LINE -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the number-line world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_CURVE -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the function-curve world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_SLOPE -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the slope world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_PEAK -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the turning-points (cubic) world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_LIMIT -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the limit (asymptote) world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_EXPO -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the exponential (doubling) world."
        @tier "domain"
      PLAY_AREA -> external {
        id : string
      }
        @description "Menu button: navigate to the area world."
        @tier "domain"
    }

    config {
      gameTitle : string = "riya"
        @label "Game Title"
        @description "Title shown at the top of the menu."
        @tier "presentation"
    }
  }

  page "/riya" as RiyaMenuPage -> RiyaMenu
}
orbital RiyaLineOrbital {
  uses Motion from "std/behaviors/std-motion-body"
  uses Gate from "std/behaviors/std-objective-flow"
  uses Particles from "std/behaviors/std-fx-particles"

  type RiyaLineBody = {
    id : string!
    x : number!
    y : number!
    vx : number
    vy : number
    ax : number
    ay : number
  }
  type RiyaLineFeature = {
    id : string
    x : number!
    y : number!
    z : number
    type : string!
    color : string
    elevation : number
    done : boolean
  }
  type RiyaLineFx = {
    id : string!
    type : string!
    x : number!
    z : number
    y : number
    message : string
    ttl : number!
  }

  entity RiyaLineState [runtime, shared] {
    id : string!
    active : boolean = false
    bodies : [RiyaLineBody] = []
    gravity : number = 0
    biasAx : number = 0
    biasAy : number = 0
    features : [RiyaLineFeature] = []
    score : number = 0
    objectivesLeft : number = 0
    result : string = "none"
    fx : [RiyaLineFx] = []
    holding : number = 0
    celebrated : boolean = false
  }

  trait LineMotion = Motion.traits.MotionBody -> RiyaLineState {
    events {
      THRUST: LINE_THRUST
      IMPULSE: LINE_IMPULSE
      PLACE: LINE_PLACE
      SET_GRAVITY: LINE_SET_GRAVITY
      RESTART: LINE_RESTART
      BODY_MOVED: LINE_MOVED
    }
    config {
      running: true
      gravity: 0
      damping: 0.94
      maxSpeed: 7
      xMin: -9
      xMax: 9
      yMin: 0
      yMax: 0
      bodies: [ { id: "hero", x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, ax: 0, ay: 0 } ]
    }

    listens {
      THRUST { id : string!, ax : number!, ay : number! }
      IMPULSE { id : string!, dvx : number!, dvy : number! }
      PLACE { id : string!, x : number!, y : number! }
      SET_GRAVITY { gravity : number! }
      SET_BIAS { biasAx : number!, biasAy : number! }
      RESTART { id : string }
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_IMPULSE -> LINE_IMPULSE
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_RESTART -> LINE_RESTART
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_THRUST -> LINE_THRUST
    }
  }

  trait LineGate = Gate.traits.ObjectiveFlow -> RiyaLineState {
    events {
      PROGRESS: LINE_PROGRESS
      GAME_END: LINE_GAME_END
      RESTART: LINE_RESTART
    }
    config { running: true }

    listens {
      PROGRESS { objectivesLeft : number, movesLeft : number }
      RESTART { id : string }
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_PROGRESS -> LINE_PROGRESS
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_RESTART -> LINE_RESTART
    }
  }

  trait LineFx = Particles.traits.FxParticles -> RiyaLineState {
    events {
      BURST: LINE_BURST
    }
    config { running: true }

    listens {
      BURST { particles : [Fx] }
      RESTART { }
      RiyaLinePlay.LINE_BURST -> LINE_BURST
    }
  }

  trait RiyaLinePlay -> @rebindable RiyaLineState [interaction, instance] {
    initial: idle

    state idle {
      INIT -> idle
        (set @entity.active true)
        (set @entity.holding 0)
        (set @entity.celebrated false)
        (set @entity.features @config.stars)
        (set @entity.score 0)
        (set @entity.objectivesLeft (array/len @config.stars))
        (emit LINE_RESTART { id: "board" })
        (render-ui main {
          type: game-shell
          appName: "riya"
          hud: { type: game-hud, stats: [ { label: @config.objectiveText }, { label: "x", value: (math/round (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) x) 1) }, { label: "v", value: (math/round (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) vx) 1) }, { label: "★", value: @entity.score } ] }
          controls: { type: control-grid, kind: "dpad", directionEvents: { left: "LINE_PAD_LEFT", right: "LINE_PAD_RIGHT" } }
          overlay: (if (!= @entity.result "none") { type: game-menu, title: @config.clearTitle, subtitle: @config.clearSubtitle, options: [ { id: "next", label: "Next ▶", event: "LINE_NEXT", variant: "primary" } ] } null)
          children: [ {
            type: math-canvas
            width: @config.width
            height: @config.height
            xMin: @config.xMin
            xMax: @config.xMax
            yMin: @config.yMin
            yMax: @config.yMax
            showTickLabels: true
            keyMap: { ArrowLeft: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT", KeyA: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT", ArrowRight: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT", KeyD: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT" }
            keyUpMap: { ArrowLeft: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT_UP", KeyA: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT_UP", ArrowRight: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT_UP", KeyD: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT_UP" }
            curves: [ { label: "", color: "#94a3b8", samples: [ { x: @config.xMin, y: 0 }, { x: @config.xMax, y: 0 } ] } ]
            points: (array/concat
              (array/map @entity.features (fn f { x: (object/get @f x), y: 0, label: "★", color: @config.starColor, radius: 9 }))
              (array/concat
                [ { x: (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) x), y: 0, label: "riya", color: @config.riyaColor, radius: 6 } ]
                (array/map @entity.fx (fn e { x: (object/get @e x), y: 0.6, label: (object/get @e message), color: "#ffe066", radius: 4 }))))
            vectors: [ { x: (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) x), y: 0, vx: (* (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) vx) 0.3), vy: 0, color: @config.riyaColor, label: "v" } ]
          } ]
        })

      LINE_PUSH_LEFT -> idle when (and (== @entity.active true) (and (== @entity.result "none") (!= @entity.holding -1)))
        (set @entity.holding -1)
        (emit LINE_THRUST { id: "hero", ax: (- 0 @config.thrust), ay: 0 })

      LINE_PUSH_RIGHT -> idle when (and (== @entity.active true) (and (== @entity.result "none") (!= @entity.holding 1)))
        (set @entity.holding 1)
        (emit LINE_THRUST { id: "hero", ax: @config.thrust, ay: 0 })

      LINE_PUSH_LEFT_UP -> idle when (== @entity.holding -1)
        (set @entity.holding 0)
        (emit LINE_THRUST { id: "hero", ax: 0, ay: 0 })

      LINE_PUSH_RIGHT_UP -> idle when (== @entity.holding 1)
        (set @entity.holding 0)
        (emit LINE_THRUST { id: "hero", ax: 0, ay: 0 })

      LINE_PAD_LEFT -> idle when (and (== @entity.active true) (== @entity.result "none"))
        (emit LINE_IMPULSE { id: "hero", dvx: (- 0 @config.padImpulse), dvy: 0 })

      LINE_PAD_RIGHT -> idle when (and (== @entity.active true) (== @entity.result "none"))
        (emit LINE_IMPULSE { id: "hero", dvx: @config.padImpulse, dvy: 0 })

      LINE_GAME_END -> idle when (and (== @payload.result "won") (== @entity.celebrated false))
        (set @entity.celebrated true)
        (emit RIYA_LEVEL_SOLVED { level: "line" })

      LINE_NEXT -> idle
        (navigate @config.nextPath)
    }

    ticks {
      gameTick every 50ms when (and (== @entity.active true) (and (== @entity.result "none") (> (array/len @entity.bodies) 0)))
        (let ((hx (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) x)))
        (let ((matched (array/filter @entity.features (fn f (<= (grid/manhattan-distance { x: (object/get @f x), y: (object/get @f y) } { x: @hx, y: 0 }) @config.reachRadius)))))
        (if (> (array/len @matched) 0)
          (do
            (set @entity.features (array/filter @entity.features (fn f (> (grid/manhattan-distance { x: (object/get @f x), y: (object/get @f y) } { x: @hx, y: 0 }) @config.reachRadius))))
            (set @entity.score (+ @entity.score (array/len @matched)))
            (set @entity.objectivesLeft (- @entity.objectivesLeft (array/len @matched)))
            (emit LINE_BURST { particles: (array/map @matched (fn f { id: (str/concat "fx-line-" (object/get @f id)), type: "pickup", x: (object/get @f x), z: (object/get @f y), message: "+1", ttl: 3 })) })
            (emit LINE_PROGRESS { objectivesLeft: @entity.objectivesLeft, movesLeft: 9999 }))
          null)))

      renderTick every 100ms when (and (== @entity.active true) (> (array/len @entity.bodies) 0))
        (render-ui main {
          type: game-shell
          appName: "riya"
          hud: { type: game-hud, stats: [ { label: @config.objectiveText }, { label: "x", value: (math/round (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) x) 1) }, { label: "v", value: (math/round (object/get (array/find @entity.bodies (fn b (== @b.id "hero"))) vx) 1) }, { label: "★", value: @entity.score } ] }
          controls: { type: control-grid, kind: "dpad", directionEvents: { left: "LINE_PAD_LEFT", right: "LINE_PAD_RIGHT" } }
          overlay: (if (!= @entity.result "none") { type: game-menu, title: @config.clearTitle, subtitle: @config.clearSubtitle, options: [ { id: "next", label: "Next ▶", event: "LINE_NEXT", variant: "primary" } ] } null)
          children: [ {
            type: math-canvas
            width: @config.width
            height: @config.height
            xMin: @config.xMin
            xMax: @config.xMax
            yMin: @config.yMin
            yMax: @config.yMax
            showTickLabels: true
            keyMap: { ArrowLeft: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT", KeyA: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT", ArrowRight: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT", KeyD: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT" }
            keyUpMap: { ArrowLeft: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT_UP", KeyA: "LINE_PUSH_LEFT_UP", ArrowRight: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT_UP", KeyD: "LINE_PUSH_RIGHT_UP" }
            curves: [ { label: "", color: "#94a3b8", samples: [ { x: @config.xMin, y: 0 }, { x: @config.xMax, y: 0 } ] } ]
            points: (array/concat
              (array/map @entity.features (fn f { x: (object/get @f x), y: 0, label: "★", color: @config.starColor, radius: 9 }))
              (array/concat
